requirement:
Arizona (AZ) PSO Services. Provision of all management, supervision, manpower, training, equipment, supplies, licenses, permits, certificates, insurance, pre-employment
screenings, reports, file and any other resources necessary to accomplish Protective Security Officer (Guard) services at FPS protected federal facilities. Typical PSO duties include: access control, visitor processing, screening, control center operation, traffic control, key control, monitor/operate security and safety systems, monitor and report on facility occupants/visitors for compliance with Federal Management Regulations and the facilities’ posted rules, maintain physical security, law and order;
reporting of hazardous conditions, summon assistance in response to injury or illness; report all potential or actual serious incidents to FPS MegaCenters; and provide necessary assistance/response to civil disturbances or emergencies.

The scope of work generally consists of interior and exterior repairs to the building structure/envelope, construction of new interior partitions, removal and replacement of low-slope roofing systems, as well as the removal and replacement of select HVAC equipment at the Ida Lewis Auditorium at Training Center Cape May. Work includes, but is not limited to:

- The repair of exterior CMU wall assembly;

- The repair of exterior concrete ramp and stairs, including tile finish;

- The construction of new interior partitions; including the installation of interior doors;

- The removal of exiting EPDM roofing system, and the installation of new modified bituminous roofing system;

- The removal of existing air handlers, boilers, condensers, insulated ductwork, dampers, and associated controls; and the installation of new air handlers, boilers, condensers, insulated ductwork, dampers, and associated controls.

- Remove existing Guard Shack at Main Gate, and install new Guard Shack at Main Gate (Pennsylvania Avenue)

- Remove existing Guard Shack at North Gate, and install new Guard Shack at North Gate (Delaware Avenue), including new power service;

- Remove existing EPDM and standing seam metal roofing systems, and install new modified bituminous and standing seam metal roofing systems at Security Building, including removal and replacement of aluminum gutters and downspouts;

- Repair existing security fence;

- Install new automatic retractable security bollards;

- Install new exterior lighting;

- Remove existing Backflow Preventer Shelter, and install new Backflow Preventer Shelter.

The scope of work generally consists of exterior repairs to the building structure/envelope at the Instruction Buildings #251 and #252 at Training Center Cape May. Work includes, but is not limited to:

- Abatement of exterior lead-based-paint;

- Repointing existing mortar joints;

- Application of new elastomeric coatings on pre-cast concrete canopies;

- Removal of existing aluminum-framed windows, and the installation of new aluminum framed windows.

The scope of work generally consists of interior finish repairs, as well as the removal and replacement of select HVAC equipment at the Gymnasium at Training Center Cape May. Work includes, but is not limited to:

- The repair of interior finishes, including floor tile and sound attenuation panels;

- The removal of existing air handlers, insulated ductwork, dampers, and associated controls; and the installation of new air handlers, insulated ductwork, dampers, and associated controls.

The scope of work generally consists of interior and exterior repairs to the building structure/envelope, removal and replacement of low-slope roofing systems, as well as the removal and replacement of select electrical equipment at IPD at Training Center Cape May. Work includes, but is not limited to:

- Removal of existing exterior aluminum-framed window and door assemblies, and the installation of new exterior aluminum-framed window and door assemblies;

- Removal of existing standing seam metal roof, and the installation of new standing seam metal roof, including the removal and replacement of existing aluminum gutters and downspouts;

- Removal and replacement of Main Distribution Panel.

The scope of work generally consists of the removal and replacement of low-slope roofing systems, as well as the removal and replacement of major HVAC equipment at the Harborview Community Club at Training Center Cape May. Work includes, but is not limited to:

- The removal of exiting EPDM roofing systems, and the installation of new modified bituminous roofing systems;

- The removal of existing aluminum gutters and downspouts, and the installation of new aluminum gutters and downspouts;

- The removal of existing air handlers, boilers, condensers, insulated ductwork, dampers, and associated controls; and the installation of new air handlers, boilers, condensers, insulated ductwork, dampers, and associated controls.

The scope of work generally consists repaving and maintenance of roads and sidewalks at Training Center Cape May. Work includes, but is not limited to:

- Mill and Overlay Diligence Avenue (from Yeaton to Scammel);

- Mill and Overlay of Massachusetts Ave (from Diligence to Munro);

- Construction of new sidewalk(s);

- Removal and replacement of stormwater inlets 

- Removal and replacement of select runs of underground utility piping;

- Seal-Coating five (5) housing parking areas.
